From e15fa10b462d628bd836826129357fbea80b37e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 18:05:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0222 -- organya title/menu pump-feed + prerender-off
 diagnostic

The v1.0.8 organya depth-regulated audio pump (pump-to-target, the TICKPUMP()
call) lived ONLY in run_tick_fixed, which gameloop() dispatches solely at
game.mode==GM_NORMAL (gameplay). The TITLE/menu (and inventory, and every other
mode) runs through the 1:1 run_tick() path, which had NO pump -- so at the title
the organya prerender ring was fed only ~1 buffer-chunk per displayed frame
(~23 ms audio per ~31 ms flip = ~74% real-time) -> the title music played slow +
distorted. Gameplay's ~2.8 chunks/frame held the 186 ms setpoint; the title never
got there. (Surfaced once the ORG_PRERENDER default-flip made organya prerender
the default -- the title is the first thing a default organya install hears.)

FIX: call the SAME bounded pump (_audio_tick_pump, the TICKPUMP() macro target)
from run_tick() too, once per displayed frame, right before the flip -- mirroring
run_tick_fixed's pump-before-render-submit placement. A forward declaration is
added because run_tick() sits above the pump's file-scope definition.

Why this is safe + correctly inert:
- The pump is RENDER-coupled (fires once per displayed frame); gameloop()
  dispatches run_tick() OR run_tick_fixed() once per loop iteration, so the title
  pump cadence matches gameplay. The "different tick cadence" is the LOGIC cadence
  (1:1 vs fixed-timestep catch-up), which does not touch the render-coupled pump.
- SAME bound: 186 ms depth setpoint + the 4-chunk per-frame cap. The cap is the
  load-bearing scheduler safety -- a bounded memcpy pump cannot monopolize the
  cooperative thread, so this cannot reintroduce a Bug-5-style title stall (Bug-5
  was a live-synth COLD-RENDER monopolizing the scheduler; this is a cache-HIT
  bounded pump, the safe opposite).
- INERT by construction off the organya prerender path: org_pump_target_ms()
  returns 0 when org_prerender_buffer_ready() is false (OPL3/WB/live-synth/
  uncached), so _audio_tick_pump no-ops -> byte-identical for those. Same
  killswitch family (SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_ORG_PUMP_TARGET_MS=0).
- No double-pump: run_tick_fixed keeps its single existing TICKPUMP(); gameloop
  dispatches exactly one of the two paths per frame.
- The pump never overlaps a 0214 render-quiesce / cold-render window: those are
  blocking calls inside Organya::start / load_stage, during which run_tick is not
  executing; the per-frame pump only runs on an already-populated buffer.
- Bonus: also feeds inventory + any other 1:1/run_tick mode that plays organya
  prerender music -- all self-gated.

RIDE-ALONG (deferred from the def-flip fix, now free since this patch already
moves BUILD_SHA12): a one-time diagnostic LOG at Organya::start's prerender-resolve
site -- when organya is active but prerender resolves OFF (live synth), emit
"organya: ORG_PRERENDER=0 -> live synth (slow on 486-class; set =1 ...)". The
SILENT absence of the pre-render banners cost a full diagnostic cycle this
campaign; this self-announces the slow path. No behavior change; killswitch intact.

NOTE: this patch changes the patch-stack DOSKUTSU_BUILD_SHA12, so the previously
deployed cache invalidates -- the 0222 binary needs a fresh make org-cache cache
(or the on-target 0221 auto-precache rebuilds it). Expected for this fix.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/main.cpp          | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/sound/Organya.cpp | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 38 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index 1d260925..d64f1dea 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -131,6 +131,12 @@ void update_fps()
 // run_tick() line is byte-unchanged.
 static int g_tick_count = 0;
 
+// patch 0222: forward-decl of the depth-regulated audio pump (defined below at
+// file scope alongside the TICKPUMP() macro). run_tick() sits ABOVE that
+// definition but needs to feed the organya prerender ring at the title/menu
+// (the 1:1 path) the same way run_tick_fixed feeds it at GM_NORMAL.
+static void _audio_tick_pump(void);
+
 static inline void run_tick()
 {
   static bool can_tick       = true;
@@ -217,6 +223,22 @@ static inline void run_tick()
       can_tick = false;
     }
 
+    // patch 0222: feed the organya prerender ring at the title/menu (+ inventory
+    // + any other 1:1/run_tick mode). The depth-regulated pump-to-target only
+    // lived in run_tick_fixed (GM_NORMAL, via TICKPUMP()), so the title ring
+    // underran (~1 pump per displayed frame = ~74% real-time -> slow + distorted
+    // title music; flush-instr g2k-quantified). This is the SAME bounded pump
+    // (186 ms depth setpoint + 4-chunk per-frame cap); the cap is the load-bearing
+    // scheduler safety -- it cannot monopolize the cooperative thread, so no
+    // Bug-5-style title stall (Bug-5 was live-synth cold-render; this is a
+    // cache-HIT bounded memcpy pump). INERT by construction off the organya
+    // prerender path: org_pump_target_ms() returns 0 when org_prerender_buffer_
+    // ready() is false (OPL3/WB/live-synth/uncached) -> _audio_tick_pump no-ops ->
+    // byte-identical there. Fires once per displayed frame (render-coupled, like
+    // run_tick_fixed); placed before the flip so the ring is topped up right
+    // before present. Same killswitch family (SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_ORG_PUMP_TARGET_MS=0).
+    _audio_tick_pump(); // == run_tick_fixed's TICKPUMP()
+
     if (settings->show_fps)
     {
       update_fps();
diff --git a/src/sound/Organya.cpp b/src/sound/Organya.cpp
index 8ad46e28..ed8e41d0 100644
--- a/src/sound/Organya.cpp
+++ b/src/sound/Organya.cpp
@@ -1273,6 +1273,22 @@ bool Organya::start(int startBeat)
   bool _prebuf = false;
   if (org_prerender_active())
     _prebuf = _organya_prerender_decide(song, startBeat);
+  else
+  {
+    // patch 0222 ride-along (task #15): organya is the active backend (Organya::
+    // start is organya-only -- opl3/wb route via MidiScheduler) but pre-render
+    // resolved OFF -> live synth, which is slow on 486-class HW and bypasses the
+    // PCM cache. Self-announce ONCE so a future ORG_PRERENDER=0 run is diagnosable
+    // straight from the log (the SILENT absence of the pre-render banners cost a
+    // full diagnostic cycle this campaign). No behavior change; killswitch intact.
+    static bool _warned_prerender_off = false;
+    if (!_warned_prerender_off)
+    {
+      _warned_prerender_off = true;
+      LOG_INFO("organya: ORG_PRERENDER=0 -> live synth (slow on 486-class; set "
+               "SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_ORG_PRERENDER=1 for cached real-time)");
+    }
+  }
   if (!_prebuf)
   {
     g_org_prerender_buf.clear();
